---
import StaticPageLayout from "../layouts/StaticPageLayout.astro";
---

<StaticPageLayout
  title="Advertising Disclosure"
  eyebrow="TRANSPARENCY"
  description="How LUDIVON plans to use advertising and maintain a clear distinction between advertisements and editorial content."
>
  <h2>How LUDIVON is funded</h2>

  <p>
    LUDIVON's approved revenue model is third-party
    display advertising.
  </p>

  <p>
    Advertising is intended to support the costs of
    operating and maintaining the publication while
    keeping its editorial guides publicly accessible.
  </p>

  <div class="prelaunch-note">
    <p>
      <strong>Current status:</strong>
      Advertising is not active in the current website
      implementation. It will only be introduced after
      separate publisher approval and the necessary
      operational and compliance checks.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Advertising network</h2>

  <p>
    Monetag is the intended initial advertising network,
    subject to account eligibility, provider requirements
    and separate activation approval.
  </p>

  <p>
    Its use must not be interpreted as confirmation that
    advertising has already been activated or that a
    particular advertising format has been approved.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and editorial independence</h2>

  <p>
    Advertisements must remain distinguishable from
    LUDIVON's editorial material.
  </p>

  <p>
    Advertising placement does not constitute evidence
    that an article, game, device, product or external
    service has been tested, endorsed or independently
    verified by LUDIVON.
  </p>

  <p>
    Editorial conclusions and technical claims must
    continue to follow our
    <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising experience</h2>

  <p>
    Any future advertising must follow these principles:
  </p>

  <ul class="policy-list">
    <li>Advertisements must be clearly distinguishable from editorial content.</li>
    <li>Ads must not imitate navigation or download controls.</li>
    <li>Ads must not obscure instructions or essential article content.</li>
    <li>Forced redirects and popunder formats are not permitted.</li>
    <li>Advertising positions should avoid unnecessary layout shifts.</li>
    <li>Advertising must not compromise readability or accessibility.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Revenue model limitations</h2>

  <p>
    LUDIVON's approved revenue model is advertising only.
  </p>

  <p>
    The publication does not plan to offer reader-paid
    subscriptions, memberships, paid ad removal or
    reader-facing advertising cancellation and billing
    functionality.
  </p>

  <p>
    Affiliate commissions are not part of the approved
    revenue model.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and advertising technologies</h2>

  <p>
    Before advertising is activated, the publisher must
    review the advertising network's data practices,
    applicable consent requirements and the changes
    required to the
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Publisher control</h2>

  <p>
    LUDIVON's advertising implementation is intended
    to include one publisher-controlled switch that
    can disable advertising across the publication.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is an operational control managed by the
    publisher. It is not a paid reader feature.
  </p>
</StaticPageLayout>